/vendor/
/composer.lock

# ⚠️ `/public/` IS TRACKED, deliberately. It is the built admin, and it
# is what a PHP application installs -- there is no Angular toolchain on
# the other side of `composer require`, so the artefact has to be in the
# package. 21.03 MB, 650 files, rewritten on every release.
#
# That cost was accepted with its eyes open. The alternatives were: make
# the 14 @coolms/* dependencies real, which is blocked on a package that
# is deliberately private and on export subpaths that are not published;
# or build it in CI, which is this same commit made by a machine and is
# where it should end up. Neither removes the need for the bytes.
#
# Before the first commit the artefact was 39.36 MB. It is 21.03 because
# the pdf.js variants no browser in this baseline can reach were pinned
# out (-10.65) and the document fonts moved to the package that owns them
# (-7.68). Both were done FIRST, on purpose: git does not forget, and the
# first commit fixes whatever is in it.

# 837M, and a symlink target for six sibling packages.
/angular/node_modules/

# 4.3G of tooling output: `out-tsc` from type-checks and a fresh `test-out/<uuid>`
# per karma run, which is never cleaned up. `angular/.gitignore` says the same
# thing for anyone reading from in there.
/angular/dist/
/angular/.angular/
/angular/coverage/

# phpunit's per-run cache
.phpunit.result.cache

# GENERATED, not authored. A prebuild step used to write here:
#   a copy of the document engine's assets/fonts directory
# before every build, so these 24 files are a copy of what
# @coolms/document-engine already ships -- byte for byte, verified.
# They were tracked here for a while, which meant a PHP consumer
# downloaded 7.71 MB of fonts that the engine owns.
angular/public/assets/document-fonts/
